<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ya'qub (Aq Qoyunlu sultan)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1463–<a href="/years/1490">1490</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Sultan Ya'qub</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ya'qub was ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a> confederation from 1478 to 1490, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzun-hasan">Uzun Hasan</a>. From his capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> he presided over a brilliant Persianate court that patronised poets and painters, and his forces helped defeat the Safavid leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaykh-haydar">Shaykh Haydar</a> in 1488. His sudden death in 1490 left the confederation divided among rival princes.</p></div>
